From: allolive <160342668+allolive@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 03 Jul 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] AML: play HDR10+ as Dolby Vision P8.1 (metadata conversion)

Adapts @cpm-code's HDR10+ to Dolby Vision conversion (from pannal/xbmc, branch
aml-4.9-21.3) to Kodi 22, keeping @pannal's switch to libdovi
dovi_generate_from_json for the RPU and @doppingkoala's histogram-based avg_pq.

On a Dolby Vision capable display, a stream carrying HDR10+ dynamic metadata is
played as Dolby Vision profile 8.1. "Tone map HDR to Dolby Vision" does not do
this: the VS10 engine tone maps from the static HDR10 values and never reads the
HDR10+ dynamic metadata.

One setting, off by default:

  Settings > CoreELEC > Convert HDR10+ to Dolby Vision
  Off (default) / CM v4.0 / CM v2.9

CM v2.9 has no field for a level 1 average below 819 codewords. CM v4.0 carries
the remainder in a level 3 offset, so it is theoretically a more accurate
representation on a display that reads level 3. This has not been measured.

Co-authored-by: cpm-code <162544069+cpm-code@users.noreply.github.com>
Co-authored-by: pannal <1359593+pannal@users.noreply.github.com>
Co-authored-by: doppingkoala <doppingkoala@users.noreply.github.com>

Downstream shaping: this was proposed upstream as CoreELEC/xbmc#86 and declined,
so it stays a downstream patch and has to survive upstream churn on its own. The
conversion therefore lives in AMLHdr10PlusHook, reached from the codec through a
handful of one-line calls, rather than inline. The behaviour is unchanged - the
moved code is the same code - but DVDVideoCodecAmlogic.cpp now carries 16 added
lines instead of 197, so upstream churn in the codec has almost nothing of ours
to collide with. CoreELEC's own m_stripHdr10Plus stays in the codec and is
passed in by reference where arming has to change it; nothing that was already
CoreELEC's moves into our file.

The one line that is modified rather than added is the native HDR10+ side
channel gate, which has to learn about conversion for the feature to work at all.

Signed-off-by: allolive <160342668+allolive@users.noreply.github.com>
